From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:16:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] use assertEqual instead of the assertEquals alias removed
 in Python 3.12

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; it affects every Python >= 3.12 test run on any architecture, so it needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

unittest's deprecated assertEquals alias was removed in Python 3.12, so
test_configuration_modify_defaults and test_slave fail with an
AttributeError before checking anything. Upstream's tox envlist stops at
py311 and never hit it; the published cp312 wheels have the same gap.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 tests/test_configuration.py | 2 +-
 tests/test_slave.py         | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/test_configuration.py b/tests/test_configuration.py
index 26b1708..5d156bb 100644
--- a/tests/test_configuration.py
+++ b/tests/test_configuration.py
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@ class TestRedisliteConfiguration(unittest.TestCase):
         self.assertIn('\ndaemonize no', result)
 
         # ensure the global defaults are not modified
-        self.assertEquals(
+        self.assertEqual(
             redislite.configuration.DEFAULT_REDIS_SETTINGS["daemonize"], "yes"
         )
 
diff --git a/tests/test_slave.py b/tests/test_slave.py
index 1cee61e..58d0d36 100644
--- a/tests/test_slave.py
+++ b/tests/test_slave.py
@@ -22,4 +22,4 @@ class TestRedisliteSlave(unittest.TestCase):
         master.set('key', 'value')
         time.sleep(.5)
         value = slave.get('key').decode(encoding='UTF-8')
-        self.assertEquals(value, 'value')
+        self.assertEqual(value, 'value')
